Alternately, it would be acceptable to combine the two variables into a three-state enum:

```suggestion
    enum class MsgState
    {
        idle = 0,
        inProgress,
        inEscape,
        max
    };
    MsgState msgState;
```

Then you have a state machine that can move from idle to inProgress on a start char, inProgress to inEscape on an escape char and then back to inProgress on the next char or back to idle on end of message.
